Phase A: Ingestion and Sensor Calibration Testing
 * Baseline Comparison: Cross-reference real-time gauge feeds from sentinel stations (e.g., Toledo, OH and Buffalo, NY) against independent secondary gauges.
 * Drift and Error Analysis: Measure sensor drift under high-velocity wind stress conditions over a standard 48-hour continuous window.
Phase B: Cryptographic and Data Pipeline Security Audit
 * Encryption Standard Verification: Confirm that telemetry packets utilize AES-256-GCM state commitments combined with post-quantum key encapsulation mechanisms (e.g., ML-KEM-1024).
 * Penetration Testing: Simulate man-in-the-middle (MitM) injection attacks on the data transport layer to verify that compromised nodes automatically fail safe without corrupting the central historical database.
Phase C: Infrastructure Simulation & Stress Testing
 * Hydrodynamic Load Testing: Subject the digital twin architecture of the coastal barriers to simulated surges exceeding historical maxima by 20%.
 * Fail-Safe Response Time: Measure the latency between automated warning triggers and the mechanical deployment of adaptive seiche mitigation barriers.
